**Read:** Complete the public MIT coursework and the assigned books/reports. Work all three investigations below: constrained structural selection, a functional/interface substitution, and a recovery/life-cycle comparison.

Use complete sources with methods, not only abstracts or material tables. Derive the governing equations, reconstruct the relevant measurement and processing conditions, and check calculations independently. Compare a changed condition not used to choose or fit the initial model. Carry uncertainty and missing evidence into the conclusion.

**Deliver:** Three substantial investigations with traceable material states, requirements, calculations, alternatives and criticism. A numerical example is a learning instrument, not proof that an actual part is qualified. Distinguish observed results, reproduced published results and new hypothetical predictions. Answer a substantive competing interpretation and revise each study.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
**Continue in materials engineering:** [Advanced study of constrained structural material selection](Advanced-study-of-constrained-structural-material-selection.lingua#r_7RHF819EVVP3F475H26NTC3S01), [Advanced study of functional material and interface substitution](Advanced-study-of-functional-material-and-interface-substitution.lingua#r_4EFHRSVJC8PB3XWWVQAG1BRWYD), [Advanced study of recovery and whole-life functional equivalence](Advanced-study-of-recovery-and-whole-life-functional-equivalence.lingua#r_1GK297HPGAR04W9W368BXG1HR8).

